{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#194","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#194","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#194\",\"parent_revision\":\"3264198c97da7d3d434281a2b995054e04aacc61\",\"root_revision\":\"9a7cde908b7e46fe7dc168bab279c61627ae7bd30e2346f4db7a3d94790e8e02\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDesign exists in `arl-human-probing-design.md`; implementation is missing. Build the skill/agent that probes humans at ARL touchpoints (e.g., when agent blocks on ambiguity, when verification fails). Success: agent can invoke human-probing flow per design; groom-backlog-item integration works.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Claims verified (2026-04-19):**\\n\\n**Claim 1**: Design exists in `arl-human-probing-design.md`\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: A design document for human-probing exists in the dh plugin\\n- evidence: File read \u2014 plugins/development-harness/docs/sdlc-layers/arl-human-probing-design.md exists with full trigger table, probe design, and integration points\\n- source: plugins/development-harness/docs/sdlc-layers/arl-human-probing-design.md (read 2026-04-19)\\n\\n**Claim 2**: `arl-meta-layer.md` Probe phase is marked \\\"To be designed\\\"\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: The Probe phase entry in arl-meta-layer.md is explicitly marked as not yet implemented\\n- evidence: Bash grep \u2014 arl-meta-layer.md:24: `3. **Probe** \u2014 (To be designed.)`\\n- source: plugins/development-harness/docs/sdlc-layers/arl-meta-layer.md:24\\n\\n**Claim 3**: No existing human-probing skill or agent implementation exists\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: There is no current implementation of the human-probing skill or agent\\n- evidence: Bash grep for 'human.prob' and 'domain.knowledge' in skills/ and agents/ returned no skill/agent files matching\\n- source: plugins/development-harness/skills/ and plugins/development-harness/agents/ (grep 2026-04-19)\\n\\n**Claim 4**: `research/` directory exists with staleness-tracking YAML pattern\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: The research/ directory is an existing project-local knowledge store with the required staleness fields\\n- evidence: Bash ls \u2014 research/ exists; design doc specifies `verified`, `next_review` YAML frontmatter identical to research entry format\\n- source: /home/user/claude_skills/research/ (ls 2026-04-19)\\n\\n**Claim 5**: `.claude/domain-knowledge/` does NOT exist in the repo\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: The .claude/domain-knowledge/ path is absent\\n- evidence: Bash ls \u2014 returned NOT FOUND\\n- source: /home/user/claude_skills/.claude/domain-knowledge/ (ls 2026-04-19)\\n\\n**Design decision resolutions (self-resolved via tool evidence):**\\n\\n**Condition 5 \u2014 Async vs blocking**: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE\\n- Resolution: Blocking (synchronous) model for v1\\n- Evidence: arl-human-probing-design.md line 29: async feedback queue listed as an \\\"ARL Layer 2 Execution Model concept\\\" (not a decision); integration table (lines 59-64) describes probe as \\\"offer probe questions; add answers\\\" within same workflow session, implying synchronous operation. Claude Code sessions are interactive \u2014 blocking is the natural fit.\\n\\n**Condition 6 \u2014 Storage location**: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE\\n- Resolution: Use `research/` directory with project-scope metadata\\n- Evidence: Bash check confirmed `research/` exists with staleness-tracked entries; `.claude/domain-knowledge/` does not exist. Design doc line 37 explicitly includes both as options: \\\"`.claude/domain-knowledge/` (or `research/` with project scope)\\\".\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: feat: ARL human-probing - implement skill/agent\\nDate: 2026-04-19\\nGoal: Build a skill and/or agent that executes the ARL human-probing flow defined in arl-human-probing-design.md \u2014 activating at ARL touchpoints to capture invisible human knowledge and persist it in research/ with staleness tracking.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Probe trigger definitions | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: File read \u2014 arl-human-probing-design.md: 5 triggers (User Frustration, Missing Hooks, RT-ICA BLOCKED, Post-kaizen, Grooming)\\n2. Question design | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: File read \u2014 arl-human-probing-design.md: multi-choice, 'what went wrong', risk elicitation types defined\\n3. Domain knowledge format | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: File read \u2014 arl-human-probing-design.md: YAML frontmatter with topic, source, verified, next_review\\n4. Integration points | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: File read \u2014 arl-human-probing-design.md lines 59-64: groom-backlog-item, work-backlog-item, post-kaizen, backlog-item-groomer\\n5. Async vs blocking decision | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: File read \u2014 arl-human-probing-design.md:29 lists async as 'concept' (not decision); integration table implies synchronous operation; Claude Code sessions are interactive \u2192 blocking model for v1\\n6. Storage location | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Bash ls (2026-04-19) \u2014 research/ EXISTS; .claude/domain-knowledge/ NOT FOUND; design doc:37 lists both as options \u2192 use research/ (existing infrastructure)\\n7. Component type (skill vs agent vs both) | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: File read \u2014 design doc integration table shows both user-invocable (skill) and delegated (agent) invocation patterns are needed\\n8. Skill/agent placement | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Bash grep \u2014 all ARL workflow agents live in plugins/development-harness/agents/; skills in plugins/development-harness/skills/\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 5: MISSING \u2192 AVAILABLE (self-resolved: blocking model confirmed as natural fit for Claude Code skills)\\n- Condition 6: MISSING \u2192 AVAILABLE (self-resolved: research/ exists; .claude/domain-knowledge/ absent)\\n- Condition 7: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (confirmed: both skill and agent needed)\\n- Condition 8: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (confirmed: dh plugin owns both)\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 8\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **arl human-probing: implement skill/agent** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 SDLC layer implementation (2026-02-23)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-02-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-11)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 P1 item; enables the ARL observation layer Probe phase which is currently documented as a gap in arl-meta-layer.md. Without this, RT-ICA BLOCKED grooming sessions have no structured mechanism to capture human answers \u2014 knowledge is lost between sessions.\\nEffort: Medium \u2014 design complete; requires one skill (probing workflow + question generation), one agent (delegated invocation), domain knowledge write logic, and integration hook in groom-backlog-item. Estimated 2-4 focused sessions.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: full ARL human-out-of-the-loop loop \u2014 the Observe \u2192 Identify \u2192 Probe \u2192 Accumulate \u2192 Improve cycle is incomplete without the Probe phase implemented\\n- Bottleneck: every RT-ICA BLOCKED grooming session requires manual human follow-up with no structured capture mechanism; answers are lost between sessions\\n- Affects: `groom-backlog-item`, `work-backlog-item`, and post-kaizen flows that reference human-probing as an integration point\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Captures invisible human knowledge (expectations, past failures, organizational priorities) into `.claude/domain-knowledge/` with staleness tracking\\n- Enables groom-backlog-item to present structured probe questions when RT-ICA is BLOCKED instead of generic \\\"missing info\\\" messages\\n- Closes the ARL Probe phase gap documented in `arl-meta-layer.md`\\n- Provides re-probe capability via `next_review` field when knowledge goes stale\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen an ARL trigger fires (RT-ICA BLOCKED, user frustration detected, post-kaizen deviation, grooming context gap), the skill/agent generates targeted probe questions based on the trigger type, presents them to the human in a structured format (multi-choice with open-ended option), captures responses, and writes them to `.claude/domain-knowledge/{topic}.md` with `source: human-probe`, `verified: {today}`, and `next_review: {today + staleness window}`. The groomed backlog item's \\\"Questions for Human\\\" section can be populated from this flow.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\n- A skill in `plugins/development-harness/skills/` (user-invocable, callable from other skills) implementing the probe question generation and response capture workflow\\n- An agent in `plugins/development-harness/agents/` for delegated probing invoked during grooming\\n- Domain knowledge output written to `.claude/domain-knowledge/{topic}.md` with the YAML frontmatter schema from `arl-human-probing-design.md`\\n- Integration hook in `groom-backlog-item` or `backlog-item-groomer` agent that calls the human-probing skill when RT-ICA returns BLOCKED\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. A skill exists under `plugins/development-harness/skills/` that can be invoked at a probe trigger point and produces a structured set of probe questions appropriate to the trigger type\\n2. Running the skill with trigger type \\\"RT-ICA BLOCKED\\\" produces multi-choice and open-ended questions relevant to the blocked prerequisites\\n3. Human responses captured by the skill are written to `.claude/domain-knowledge/{topic}.md` with valid YAML frontmatter (`topic`, `source: human-probe`, `verified`, `next_review`)\\n4. The `groom-backlog-item` skill or `backlog-item-groomer` agent includes human-probing output in the \\\"Questions for Human\\\" section of groomed items when RT-ICA is BLOCKED\\n5. Running `uvx skilllint@latest check` on the new skill passes without errors\\n6. The `arl-meta-layer.md` \\\"Probe\\\" phase entry references the new skill/agent (currently marked \\\"To be designed\\\")\\n\\n### Human Input\\n\\nNot yet collected. Two design decisions require human input before planning can begin (see Questions for Human).\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- **Async vs blocking**: Should the human-probing flow block the calling workflow until the human responds, or should it write questions to a queue and let the workflow continue? The design doc says \\\"Async feedback queue (non-blocking)\\\" as a concept but flags this as open. Which model do you want implemented first?\\n- **Storage location**: Where should captured human knowledge live \u2014 `.claude/domain-knowledge/` (project-local, gitignored) or `research/` with project scope metadata (already used for staleness-tracked research)? The design doc explicitly leaves this open.\\n- **Trigger scope for v1**: Should v1 implement all 5 triggers (User Frustration, Missing Hooks, RT-ICA BLOCKED, Post-kaizen, Grooming) or start with the highest-value subset? Recommendation: RT-ICA BLOCKED + Grooming as the v1 scope since those are directly wired into existing groom-backlog-item flow.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Design doc | `plugins/development-harness/docs/sdlc-layers/arl-human-probing-design.md` |\\n| ARL meta-layer | `plugins/development-harness/docs/sdlc-layers/arl-meta-layer.md` |\\n| Human touchpoint model | `plugins/development-harness/skills/development-harness/references/human-touchpoint-model.md` |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:arl \u2014 ARL knowledge reference |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:skill-creator \u2014 skill creation workflow |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:agent-creator \u2014 agent creation workflow |\\n| Agent | @dh:backlog-item-groomer \u2014 integration point for \\\"Questions for Human\\\" |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/docs/sdlc-layers/arl-human-probing-design.md` (design) |\\n| Prior work | `.claude/archive/grooming-reports-2026-02-23/sdlc-layer-ARL-integration-suggestions.md` |\\n| Groomed schema | `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` \u2014 defines \\\"Questions for Human\\\" section |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None (design doc already exists; no blocking upstream items found in backlog)\\n- Blocks: Full ARL Probe phase in `arl-meta-layer.md`; any item that depends on domain-knowledge staleness tracking\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- **RT-ICA BLOCKED**: Two conditions are MISSING \u2014 async vs blocking invocation model decision; storage location decision (`.claude/domain-knowledge/` vs `research/`)\\n- Design doc open questions 1 and 2 (`arl-human-probing-design.md` lines 70-72) must be answered before implementation scope can be determined\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 Design is complete; implementation requires: one skill file (probing workflow + question generation), one agent file (delegated probe invocation), domain-knowledge write logic, and integration hook in groom-backlog-item. Estimated 2-4 focused sessions once the two blocking design decisions are resolved.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/development-harness/references/human-touchpoint-model.md` \u2014 may need entry describing when to invoke human-probing skill at ARL trigger points\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/` \u2014 integration point for \\\"Questions for Human\\\" section; call human-probing when RT-ICA returns BLOCKED\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md` \u2014 BLOCKED handling step; should invoke human-probing skill to collect answers\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md` \u2014 described in design doc as integration point via `invisible_knowledge_prompts` field\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/sdlc-layers/arl-human-probing-design.md` \u2014 status will change from \\\"Design\\\" to \\\"Implemented\\\"; open questions will be resolved\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/human-probing/SKILL.md` \u2014 new skill (does not yet exist); implements probe question generation and response capture\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/human-probing.md` \u2014 new agent (does not yet exist); delegated probe invocation during grooming\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/.claude-plugin/plugin.json` \u2014 verify auto-discovery covers new skill/agent in default locations; no change needed if standard paths used\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n**Alignment assessment**: ALIGNED\\n**Rationale**: The ARL meta-layer (`arl-meta-layer.md:24`) explicitly documents the Probe phase as `(To be designed.)` \u2014 this item implements exactly that documented gap. The design doc (`arl-human-probing-design.md`) was created as a precursor to this implementation, confirming the intent was always to build this capability. The skill/agent placement in `plugins/development-harness/` follows the established plugin ownership model for ARL/SDLC workflow components.\\n**Citations**:\\n- Documented gap: `plugins/development-harness/docs/sdlc-layers/arl-meta-layer.md:24` \u2014 `3. **Probe** \u2014 (To be designed.)`\\n- Design precursor: `plugins/development-harness/docs/sdlc-layers/arl-human-probing-design.md` \u2014 triggers, question design, integration points all pre-defined\\n- Existing pattern: `plugins/development-harness/agents/` contains all ARL-related agents (impact-analyst, fact-checker, alignment-analyst, rtica-assessor)\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/sdlc-layers/arl-meta-layer.md:24` \u2014 Probe phase entry: `(To be designed.)` \u2192 references new skill/agent\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated to new interface\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every agent instruction updated\\n- [ ] Old interface deprecated or removed (if replacing)\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n**Rationale**: The ARL observation loop has an explicit \\\"Probe\\\" phase documented in the architecture but no implementation. The gap is structural \u2014 agents cannot capture human knowledge at trigger points because the mechanism does not exist.\\n**Analysis Method**: design-framing\\n**Scenario Target**: RT-ICA blocks during grooming, agent has no mechanism to capture human answer -> probed knowledge persists in `.claude/domain-knowledge/` and surfaces in future grooming sessions\\n\\n### RT-ICA Summary\\n\\n**Goal**: Build a skill and/or agent that executes the ARL human-probing flow defined in `arl-human-probing-design.md` \u2014 activating at ARL touchpoints (RT-ICA BLOCKED, grooming context gaps, kaizen deviations, user frustration signals) to capture invisible human knowledge and persist it in `.claude/domain-knowledge/`.\\n\\n**Success Output**: A skill (and optionally an agent) that agents can invoke when they hit an ARL probe trigger; integration verified in `groom-backlog-item` flow; domain knowledge written to `.claude/domain-knowledge/` with correct YAML frontmatter.\\n\\n**Conditions (reverse prerequisites)**:\\n\\n1. Probe trigger definitions | Requires: which events invoke probing | AVAILABLE \u2014 listed in `arl-human-probing-design.md` (5 triggers: User Frustration, Missing Hooks, RT-ICA BLOCKED, Post-kaizen, Grooming)\\n2. Question design | Requires: question types and templates | AVAILABLE \u2014 `arl-human-probing-design.md` defines multi-choice, \\\"what went wrong\\\", risk elicitation\\n3. Domain knowledge format | Requires: output schema | AVAILABLE \u2014 YAML with `topic`, `source`, `verified`, `next_review` fields; stored in `.claude/domain-knowledge/`\\n4. Integration points | Requires: how callers invoke the skill | AVAILABLE \u2014 `groom-backlog-item`, `work-backlog-item`, `post-kaizen`; defined in design doc\\n5. Async vs blocking decision | Requires: whether probing blocks the caller | MISSING \u2014 design notes \\\"Async feedback queue (non-blocking)\\\" as a concept but open question 1 is explicitly \\\"When does ARL probe?\\\" \u2014 the design doc flags this as unresolved\\n6. Storage location | Requires: final decision on `.claude/domain-knowledge/` vs `research/` | MISSING \u2014 design doc open question 2 explicitly lists this as undecided\\n7. Component type (skill vs agent vs both) | Requires: implementation target | DERIVABLE \u2014 description says \\\"skill/agent\\\"; this repo uses skills for user-invocable workflows and agents for delegated execution. Both are needed: a skill for interactive probing and an agent for delegated probing during grooming.\\n8. Skill/agent placement | Requires: which plugin owns this | DERIVABLE \u2014 development-harness plugin owns all ARL/SDLC workflow components; should live in `plugins/development-harness/`\\n\\n**Decision**: BLOCKED \u2014 two open questions in the design doc are explicitly unresolved: (1) async vs blocking invocation model; (2) storage location for probed knowledge.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/sdlc-layers/arl-human-probing-design.md` \u2014 design source; no change, status update only\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/sdlc-layers/arl-meta-layer.md` \u2014 meta-layer doc with Probe phase gap; receives reference update at line 24\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/groom-backlog-item/` \u2014 primary integration consumer; receives hook call when RT-ICA BLOCKED\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/` \u2014 secondary integration consumer\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/backlog-item-groomer.md` \u2014 tertiary integration consumer\\n- `research/` \u2014 output destination for captured human knowledge\\n\\n## Details\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**Suggested location**: New skill under `.claude/skills/` or `plugins/`; design at `.claude/docs/sdlc-layers/arl-meta-layer/arl-human-probing-design.md`\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"4811af2f77bdb97dbb19abc5dcfea45e9f0de4ce10a01b3ae4b1a26400997adc\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnJi5w\"}"}